From 98f91ea8cc5d75b718f772acb66d24459b3242d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:38:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kernel): meter truck's faces in the STEP bench so a
 runaway face is refused

The release gate of the v0.20.0 cut hung in step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name
on bspline_discontinuous.step. solidcore reads and meshes that file in a few
milliseconds. The bench's own truck reader called robust_triangulation with
no meter: truck's subdivision does not end on a discontinuous B-spline, and
truck reads no cancel token, so the time bound had no effect.

The bench now wraps each face in a metered surface (tests/step_util/
truck_guard.rs, the bench copy of the crates/app meter from #1536). Past
25 M evaluations, or after the cancel, the face is refused by name. The
three fixtures without verdict rows (bspline_discontinuous, bspline_dome,
fillet_corner) get rows. truck-topology becomes a dev-dependency (workspace
pin) for CompressedShell. The library is not changed.

Fixes #1697

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
